 "note": "Reviewed vocabulary that maps card-eligibility wording in OFFICIAL campaign terms (and official structured card_type tokens) to canonical scope. 'product' = an explicitly named canonical product. 'family' = a stable card family/program code from master data (eligibility_master.v1.json cardFamilies); the campaign rule stays family-level and owned products match through master-data membership, so a new member product needs no campaign change. 'broad' families are bank-wide/feature-wide wording (e.g. 'Bonus özellikli bireysel kredi kartları'); they yield to an explicit exclusivity to another family. 'other' = a real card family not in master data (kept, never applied). 'platform' = a parent platform whose inclusion of our cards is not stated (needs_review). Free text never creates products or families. Patterns are Python regexes on Turkish-lowercased text, matched only in the title and in sentence-length lines. Coordinated lists ('Axess, Wings, Free ve banka kartları') are matched when a card noun follows within the clause.",
